Subject: Gambatte: Game Boy link cable over RetroArch netplay (netpacket) with timing compensation (v4bw)
Series-Step: 1/5 (gambatte link v5irh3)
Origin: hanbang (this project); record name hanbang_gb_netlink_v4bw.patch, full patch against 4041d5a
요약: 넷플레이 방을 게임보이 통신선으로 쓰는 hb_netpacket_serial.h 를 새로 넣고, 게임별 시간 제한 때문에 끊기던 것(바이트 사이 시간 맞춤)과 감바테 자체 버그 둘(직렬 바이트 밀림 · 부트롬 중 리셋)을 고침. 원본 위에 한 번에 얹는 누적 패치(v2 ~ v4bw).

New libretro netpacket serial transport (libgambatte/libretro/hb_netpacket_serial.h, protocol
"gambatte-hb-link-6", RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_SET_NETPACKET_INTERFACE). One player hosts a RetroArch netplay room, the other
joins it; each side keeps running its own game and its own save, only serial bytes travel. Outside a netplay room
nothing changes (the TCP "GB Link" options still work). Only two players; a third one is refused.

Transport and timing (accumulated v2 .. v4bw):
- every byte carries the Game Boy time its sender let pass since its previous byte (32-bit gap). The receiver guesses
  the next gap, then waits for the byte with its game paused (at most 40 ms; after the first byte of a run or an unseen gap
  at most one 240 Hz tick). A Game Boy that is behind the sender runs on until the time the byte was sent, then answers.
- the first byte of an incoming run gets a half-frame allowance once; a byte that comes soon after one this side sent is
  taken as the other side's turn and is not waited for (Tetris DX versus).
- a send gives up after 5 s and returns 0xFF; the other side drops that byte if it has not read it yet.
- core option gambatte_netlink_timing = auto | v3j | bounded. "bounded" keeps a session-wide virtual time plus progress
  notes so that one side cannot run ahead; auto selects it for three beatmania GB ROMs (identified by size + CRC32).
- cold-start barrier: both sides restart together (20 s limit). RetroArch's netplay client runs frames before the core's
  start() is called, so a start() within 1800 frames of loading restarts the game cold (SRAM/RTC kept) and waits.
- v4bw rules: a byte received late counts as received at its due time (beatmania, Bikkuri Nekketsu Shin Kiroku);
  a peer that does not listen (SC not armed for an external clock) answers FF after two frames; simultaneous sends
  resolve host-first; after a byte answered by a byte of its own the sender waits up to one tick for the next one
  (Monster Capsule GB).

Fixes in the emulation core itself:
- Memory::updateSerial (HAVE_NETWORK): bits of the incoming byte were shifted in from the top every time, so a game that
  reads SB/SC/IF while a byte is on the wire received it rotated (0x20 became 0x08). The remaining bits are now taken
  after the ones already shifted in.
- GB::reset(): call bootloader.call_FF50() before full_init(), otherwise a reset while the boot ROM is still mapped makes
  the boot ROM itself the "cartridge backup" and the game never comes back.

---
diff --git a/libgambatte/libretro/hb_netpacket_serial.h b/libgambatte/libretro/hb_netpacket_serial.h
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..6bb818dcbe53
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libgambatte/libretro/hb_netpacket_serial.h
@@ -0,0 +1,731 @@
+#ifndef HB_NETPACKET_SERIAL_H
+#define HB_NETPACKET_SERIAL_H
+
+/* Hanbang pack (2026-10-08): Game Boy link cable over RetroArch netplay.
+ *
+ * With this, link games (Pokemon trades and battles, 2P Tetris, ...) connect
+ * the same way as GBA (gpSP) and DS (melonDS DS): one player hosts a netplay
+ * room, the other joins it. Each side keeps running its own game and save; only
+ * the serial bytes travel, as RetroArch "netpacket" packets.
+ *
+ * The exchange follows NetSerial (net_serial.cpp, the TCP 'GB Link' options):
+ * the side that starts a transfer with its internal clock sends its byte and
+ * waits for the next byte from the other side; a side waiting on the external
+ * clock answers a received byte with its own. Differences:
+ *  - a send gives up after HB_NP_TIMEOUT_MS and returns 0xFF ("nobody on the
+ *    cable"), as the netpacket API asks, instead of freezing forever. It also
+ *    tells the other side to drop that byte if it has not read it yet, and a
+ *    late answer to it is ignored, so the byte stream stays in step.
+ *  - only two players: a third one trying to join the room is refused.
+ *  - (2026-10-15) timing. Each Game Boy runs a whole frame in a burst and then
+ *    sleeps, so without help the waiting side sees the bytes of a transfer a
+ *    frame or more apart, and games with a time limit between bytes give up
+ *    (Yu-Gi-Oh! DM1, Metal Gear Ghost Babel VS battle). So each byte carries
+ *    the Game Boy time its sender let pass since its previous byte. The
+ *    waiting side guesses the next gap from the gaps so far (games repeat
+ *    them: one byte a frame, or a fixed round such as 3 bytes a frame), and
+ *    once that much of its own Game Boy time has passed after answering, it
+ *    waits for the next byte with its game paused (up to HB_NP_WAIT_MS). Both
+ *    games then see about the same gaps as on a cable. After the first byte,
+ *    or a gap not seen before, it waits after one 240 Hz timer tick at most.
+ *  - (2026-10-15) the other way round: a Game Boy that is behind the sender
+ *    (it waited for a byte that did not come, or found it already queued)
+ *    runs on until it reaches the time the byte was sent, then answers; the
+ *    sender is paused until then anyway. The gap is counted from the last byte
+ *    either way and sent as 32 bits (World Heroes 2 Jet: after the 4-second VS
+ *    screen the waiting side was 2 frames behind, answered from the wrong
+ *    screen and the game reset; during a fight it fell 2.8 frames behind in 43
+ *    bytes and reset when the round ended).
+ *  - (2026-10-15) startup uncertainty: the first byte is discovered by polling,
+ *    not at an independently scheduled cable edge. The full gap alone cannot
+ *    preserve the first byte phase relative to the receiving main loop. Use
+ *    a half normal-speed frame allowance ONCE, for the first short gap of
+ *    an incoming run. Preserve the rest of that gap; do not collapse it to
+ *    zero (Beach Volley needs its main loop to see the first byte). Subsequent
+ *    bytes and long gaps retain full catch-up, so no per-byte drift is added.
+ *    This is a bounded compatibility policy, not cycle-exact cable emulation.
+ *  - (2026-10-15) a byte that comes soon after one this side sent may only be
+ *    the other side's turn: when both send in turn (Tetris DX VS: one byte each
+ *    a frame), its next byte comes after this side's next one. So after such a
+ *    byte this side does not wait for another, and its gap is not used to guess
+ *    (the wait ran out every frame and slowed the hosting Game Boy to a third).
+ * Outside a netplay session nothing changes (the GB Link options still work). */
+
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <time.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <libretro.h>
+#include <gambatte.h>
+#include "gambatte_log.h"
+
+#ifndef RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_SET_NETPACKET_INTERFACE
+#define RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_SET_NETPACKET_INTERFACE 78
+#define RETRO_NETPACKET_UNRELIABLE  0
+#define RETRO_NETPACKET_RELIABLE    (1 << 0)
+#define RETRO_NETPACKET_UNSEQUENCED (1 << 1)
+#define RETRO_NETPACKET_FLUSH_HINT  (1 << 2)
+#define RETRO_NETPACKET_BROADCAST 0xFFFF
+typedef void (RETRO_CALLCONV *retro_netpacket_send_t)(int flags, const void* buf, size_t len, uint16_t client_id);
+typedef void (RETRO_CALLCONV *retro_netpacket_poll_receive_t)();
+typedef void (RETRO_CALLCONV *retro_netpacket_start_t)(uint16_t client_id, retro_netpacket_send_t send_fn, retro_netpacket_poll_receive_t poll_receive_fn);
+typedef void (RETRO_CALLCONV *retro_netpacket_receive_t)(const void* buf, size_t len, uint16_t client_id);
+typedef void (RETRO_CALLCONV *retro_netpacket_stop_t)(void);
+typedef void (RETRO_CALLCONV *retro_netpacket_poll_t)(void);
+typedef bool (RETRO_CALLCONV *retro_netpacket_connected_t)(uint16_t client_id);
+typedef void (RETRO_CALLCONV *retro_netpacket_disconnected_t)(uint16_t client_id);
+struct retro_netpacket_callback
+{
+   retro_netpacket_start_t        start;
+   retro_netpacket_receive_t      receive;
+   retro_netpacket_stop_t         stop;
+   retro_netpacket_poll_t         poll;
+   retro_netpacket_connected_t    connected;
+   retro_netpacket_disconnected_t disconnected;
+   const char* protocol_version;
+};
+#endif
+
+#define HB_NP_PROTOCOL   "gambatte-hb-link-6"  /* v4bt: typed, generation-tagged cold-boot/reset barrier (v4bu: same wire format) */
+#define HB_NP_UNIT_LEN   25       /* type, seq(2), data, flags, gap(4), timestamp(8), own generation(4), peer generation(4), little endian */
+#define HB_NP_TIMEOUT_MS 5000    /* longest a send waits for the other Game Boy */
+#define HB_NP_QUEUE      1024    /* received units not read yet (power of two) */
+#define HB_NP_WAIT_MS    40      /* longest a waiting Game Boy stays paused for the byte it expects */
+#define HB_NP_GAP_UNIT   16      /* cycles per unit of the gap sent with a byte */
+#define HB_NP_GAP_NONE   0xFFFFFFFFu  /* first byte: nothing to count from */
+#define HB_NP_GAP_LONG   0xFFFF  /* units (about 15 frames): a gap this long starts a new run of bytes */
+#define HB_NP_STARTUP_SLACK 35112UL /* half a normal-speed frame; once per incoming run */
+#define HB_NP_CATCHUP    2106720 /* cycles (30 frames): a Game Boy further behind the sender than this answers at once */
+#define HB_NP_LATE       140448  /* two frames of cycles: a byte later than this after its expected time is not waited for */
+#define HB_NP_HIST       16      /* gaps remembered to guess the next one */
+#define HB_NP_POLL_LATE  16512   /* v4bw: cycles (two 4128-cycle runs at double speed): a byte accepted at most this
+                                  * long after it was due counts as on time (the core only checks an armed port at its
+                                  * events, so a game polling RAM saw each byte up to a run late, and the lateness piled
+                                  * up: Bikkuri Nekketsu's waiting Game Boy slipped 9 lines a frame until a bank switch
+                                  * raced its LY 112 sound interrupt and it restarted) */
+#define HB_NP_UNARMED    140448  /* v4bw: cycles (two frames, one at double speed) a byte may wait while this side does not
+                                  * listen before it gets FF back (Monster Capsule GB calls with $60 every 16 frames and
+                                  * listens in between; held 5 s, its call crossed the other player's) */
+#define HB_NP_GAP_NEW    1088    /* units (17408 cycles, one 240 Hz timer tick): the most a waiting Game Boy runs on
+                                  * after the first byte of a transfer or after a gap it has not seen before, so it
+                                  * does not run ahead of a sender that sends again soon (Pokemon TCG: the receiver
+                                  * gives up after 4 ticks without a byte, the sender waits 20 ms once after $29/$12) */
+
+#define HB_NP_BOOT_WAIT_MS 20000UL
+/* v4bu (2026-10-18, device): a RetroArch CLIENT runs frames before its netpacket start() (the host does not),
+ * so v4bt never let the client into the cold barrier and both menus lost VERSUS. A Game Boy that ran less than
+ * this many frames since its ROM loaded (and loaded no state) now restarts itself into the cold barrier at start(),
+ * and a solo Game Boy restarts when a newly joined peer offers a cold boot (bounded = the three beatmania ROMs). */
+#define HB_NP_AUTO_COLD_RUNS 1800UL
+#define HB_NP_EV_LINKED 1
+#define HB_NP_EV_SOLO 2
+#define HB_NP_EV_PEER_JOIN 3
+
+class NetpacketSerial : public gambatte::SerialIO
+{
+public:
+   NetpacketSerial() : send_fn_(NULL), poll_fn_(NULL), peer_(-1), is_host_(false),
+      seq_(0), head_(0), tail_(0), last_poll_ms_(0), clock_(0), last_xfer_clock_(0),
+      expect_(0), held_seq_(0x10000), hist_n_(0), after_send_(false), trace_(NULL), peer_clock_(0), sent_clock_(0), peer_seen_(false), sent_progress_(false), epoch_(0), epoch_set_(false), timing_(false), fresh_(true), boot_pending_(false), link_ready_(false), peer_boot_(false), generation_(0), peer_generation_(0), used_peer_generation_(0), peer_ack_(0), boot_reset_(false), peer_boot_reset_(false), boot_deadline_(0), boot_tx_ms_(0), runs_(0), auto_cold_(false), state_loaded_(false), event_(0), progressed_(false), ever_linked_(false), armed_clock_(0), late_(0), unarmed_from_(0), unarmed_seq_(0x10000), turn_seen_(false) {}
+
+   /* v4bv: automatic cold start is confined to the untouched startup window.
+    * Input delivered to a running game, a loaded state, or an established
+    * link closes that window. Explicit local reset remains user-authorized. */
+   void loaded() { fresh_=true; runs_=0; auto_cold_=false; state_loaded_=false; progressed_=ever_linked_=false; }
+   void noteInput(unsigned buttons) {
+      if (buttons && !waitingForBoot()) progressed_=true;
+   }
+   bool canAutoCold() const {
+      return !state_loaded_ && !progressed_ && !ever_linked_ && runs_ < HB_NP_AUTO_COLD_RUNS;
+   }
+   void stateLoaded() {
+      fresh_=false; state_loaded_=true; auto_cold_=false;
+      if (timeline() && started()) {
+         boot_pending_=false; link_ready_=false; clear();
+         if (peer_ >= 0) put('D',0,0,0,0);
+         debugState("state-loaded-link-suspended");
+      }
+   }
+   void localReset() {
+      debugState("before-local-reset");
+      clear();
+      if (timeline() && started()) {
+         ++generation_; if (!generation_) ++generation_;
+         boot_pending_=true; link_ready_=false; boot_reset_=true;
+         boot_deadline_=now_ms()+HB_NP_BOOT_WAIT_MS; boot_tx_ms_=0;
+      }
+      fresh_=true; runs_=0; progressed_=ever_linked_=false;
+      debugState("after-local-reset");
+   }
+   bool beforeRun() {
+      bool run = beforeRunInner();
+      if (run && runs_ < 0xFFFFFFFFUL) ++runs_;
+      return run;
+   }
+   /* v4bu: the Game Boy was just reset (SRAM/RTC kept by the caller) to enter a cold barrier */
+   void coldRestarted() {
+      clear();
+      if (timeline() && started()) {
+         if (!fresh_) { ++generation_; if (!generation_) ++generation_; }
+         boot_pending_=true; link_ready_=false; boot_reset_=false;
+         boot_deadline_=now_ms()+HB_NP_BOOT_WAIT_MS; boot_tx_ms_=0;
+      }
+      fresh_=true; runs_=0;
+      debugState("auto-cold-restart");
+   }
+   bool takeAutoCold() { bool a=auto_cold_ && timeline() && started() && canAutoCold(); auto_cold_=false; return a; }
+   int takeEvent() { int e=event_; event_=0; return e; }
+   unsigned long bootLeftMs() const { if (!boot_pending_) return 0; unsigned long n=now_ms(); return boot_deadline_>n ? boot_deadline_-n : 0; }
+   bool beforeRunInner() {
+      if (!timeline() || !started() || !boot_pending_) { fresh_=false; return true; }
+      poll_fn_();
+      unsigned long now=now_ms();
+      if (now >= boot_deadline_) {
+         boot_pending_=false; link_ready_=false; fresh_=false;
+         if (peer_ >= 0) put('D',0,0,0,0);
+         debugState("boot-timeout-solo"); event_=HB_NP_EV_SOLO;
+         return true;
+      }
+      if (peer_ >= 0) {
+         if (!boot_tx_ms_ || now-boot_tx_ms_ >= 100) {
+            put('B',0,boot_reset_ ? 1 : 0,0,0); boot_tx_ms_=now;
+         }
+         if (peer_boot_ && peer_boot_reset_==boot_reset_ && peer_generation_ != used_peer_generation_ && peer_ack_==generation_) {
+            /* Cold-start readiness is NOT consent for a later explicit reset.
+             * Matching kinds prevents an old cold offer from releasing the
+             * first reset while the user is still resetting the other side.
+             * This last echo lets the other matching endpoint pass too. */
+            put('B',0,boot_reset_ ? 1 : 0,0,0);
+            used_peer_generation_=peer_generation_;
+            boot_pending_=false; link_ready_=true; fresh_=false; ever_linked_=true;
+            debugState("boot-release"); event_=HB_NP_EV_LINKED;
+            return true;
+         }
+      }
+      return false;
+   }
+   bool waitingForBoot() const { return timeline() && boot_pending_; }
+   void debugState(const char *why) {
+      if (trace_) fprintf(trace_, "STATE %s clock=%lu epoch=%llu epoch_set=%d peer_clock=%llu peer_seen=%d sent=%llu queue=%u expect=%lu held=%u hist=%u after_send=%d seq=%u gen=%u peer_gen=%u peer_ack=%u pending=%d ready=%d kind=%d peer_kind=%d\n",
+         why,clock_,(unsigned long long)epoch_,epoch_set_,(unsigned long long)peer_clock_,peer_seen_,(unsigned long long)sent_clock_,(tail_-head_)&(HB_NP_QUEUE-1),expect_,held_seq_,hist_n_,after_send_,seq_,generation_,peer_generation_,peer_ack_,boot_pending_,link_ready_,boot_reset_,peer_boot_reset_);
+   }
+
+   void setTiming(bool enabled) { if (!started()) timing_ = enabled; }
+
+   /* netplay session callbacks */
+   void start(uint16_t client_id, retro_netpacket_send_t send_fn, retro_netpacket_poll_receive_t poll_fn)
+   {
+      send_fn_ = send_fn;
+      poll_fn_ = poll_fn;
+      is_host_ = client_id == 0;
+      peer_    = is_host_ ? -1 : 0;     /* a client only talks to the host (id 0) */
+      clear();
+      /* Optional diagnostics, explicitly selected directory; no file writes by default. */
+      const char *trace_dir = getenv("HB_NP_TRACE_DIR");
+      if (!trace_dir && access("/tmp/hb_np_trace", W_OK) == 0) trace_dir = "/tmp/hb_np_trace"; /* device RAM, only if made by hand */
+      if (!trace_ && trace_dir) {
+         char path[1024]; snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%s/np_%d.tsv", trace_dir, getpid());
+         trace_ = fopen(path, "a");
+         if (trace_)
+            setvbuf(trace_, NULL, _IOLBF, 0);
+      }
+      generation_=1; peer_generation_=used_peer_generation_=peer_ack_=0;
+      peer_boot_=false; link_ready_=false; boot_reset_=peer_boot_reset_=false;
+      boot_pending_=timeline() && !state_loaded_ && !progressed_ && (fresh_ || canAutoCold());
+      auto_cold_=boot_pending_ && !fresh_;   /* v4bu: restart first, then wait (see HB_NP_AUTO_COLD_RUNS) */
+      boot_deadline_=now_ms()+HB_NP_BOOT_WAIT_MS; boot_tx_ms_=0;
+      tr("start", is_host_ ? 1 : 0, 0, 0);
+      debugState("session-start");
+   }
+   void stop()
+   {
+      tr("stop", 0, 0, 0);
+      send_fn_ = NULL; poll_fn_ = NULL; peer_ = -1; clear();
+      boot_pending_=link_ready_=peer_boot_=false; auto_cold_=false;
+      if (trace_) { fclose(trace_); trace_ = NULL; }
+   }
+   bool started() const { return send_fn_ != NULL; }
+   bool connected(uint16_t client_id)
+   {
+      if (!is_host_ || peer_ >= 0)
+         return false;                  /* the cable has two ends */
+      peer_ = client_id;
+      clear();
+      peer_generation_=used_peer_generation_=peer_ack_=0; peer_boot_=false; link_ready_=false;
+      debugState("transport-connected");
+      return true;
+   }
+   void disconnected(uint16_t client_id)
+   {
+      if (peer_ == (int)client_id) { peer_ = -1; clear(); link_ready_=peer_boot_=false; debugState("transport-disconnected"); }
+   }
+   void receive(const void* buf, size_t len, uint16_t client_id)
+   {
+      const unsigned char* p = (const unsigned char*)buf;
+      if (peer_ < 0 || (int)client_id != peer_ || len != (timeline() ? HB_NP_UNIT_LEN : 17))
+         return;
+      unsigned seq = p[1] | (p[2] << 8);
+      uint64_t at = 0;
+      for (unsigned i=0;i<8;i++) at |= (uint64_t)p[9+i] << (8*i);
+      if (((p[4] & 0x40) != 0) != timeline()) {
+         tr("mode-mismatch",seq,p[3],0);
+         return;
+      }
+      if (timeline()) {
+         uint32_t gen=0,ack=0;
+         for (unsigned i=0;i<4;++i) { gen|=(uint32_t)p[17+i]<<(8*i); ack|=(uint32_t)p[21+i]<<(8*i); }
+         if (p[0]=='B') {
+            if (gen < peer_generation_) { tr("stale-boot",gen,0,ack); return; }
+            if (gen != peer_generation_) {
+               if (link_ready_) { link_ready_=false; clear(); }
+               peer_generation_=gen; peer_boot_=true; peer_ack_=ack; peer_boot_reset_=p[3] != 0;
+               debugState("peer-boot");
+               if (boot_pending_) { put('B',0,boot_reset_ ? 1 : 0,0,0); boot_tx_ms_=now_ms(); }
+               else if (!peer_boot_reset_ && canAutoCold()) {
+                  /* A late peer may restart only untouched, unlinked startup.
+                   * Never discard player progress or restart an old session. */
+                  auto_cold_=true; event_=HB_NP_EV_PEER_JOIN; debugState("peer-cold-join");
+               }
+            } else { peer_ack_=ack; }
+            return;
+         }
+         if (p[0]=='D') {
+            if (gen >= peer_generation_) {
+               peer_generation_=gen; peer_boot_=false; link_ready_=false; clear();
+               debugState("peer-link-suspended");
+            }
+            return;
+         }
+         if ((!link_ready_ && !boot_pending_) || !peer_boot_ || gen!=peer_generation_ || ack!=generation_) {
+            tr("stale-generation",gen,p[3],ack); return;
+         }
+         if (!peer_seen_ || at > peer_clock_) peer_clock_ = at;
+         peer_seen_ = true;
+      }
+      if (p[0] == 'P') return;
+      if (p[0] == 'C') {                /* the sender gave up on that byte: drop it if still unread */
+         for (unsigned i = head_; i != tail_; i = (i + 1) & (HB_NP_QUEUE - 1))
+            if (q_[i].type == 'Q' && q_[i].seq == seq)
+               q_[i].type = 0;
+         return;
+      }
+      if (p[0] != 'Q' && p[0] != 'R')
+         return;
+      unsigned gap = (unsigned)p[5] | ((unsigned)p[6] << 8) | ((unsigned)p[7] << 16) | ((unsigned)p[8] << 24);
+      tr(p[0] == 'Q' ? "rxQ" : "rxR", seq, p[3], gap);
+      unsigned next = (tail_ + 1) & (HB_NP_QUEUE - 1);
+      if (next == head_)
+         return;                        /* cannot happen in practice: one byte waits for one answer */
+      q_[tail_].type = p[0];
+      q_[tail_].seq  = seq;
+      q_[tail_].data = p[3];
+      q_[tail_].flag = p[4];
+      q_[tail_].gap  = gap;
+      q_[tail_].at = at;
+      tail_ = next;
+   }
+
+   /* gambatte::SerialIO */
+   virtual void setClock(unsigned long cycles) {
+      if (timeline() && epoch_set_ && cycles < epoch_) {
+         /* Never let an unannounced time rewind become UINT64_MAX lead. */
+         debugState("clock-rewind-link-suspended");
+         link_ready_=false; clear();
+         if (started() && peer_ >= 0) put('D',0,0,0,0);
+      }
+      clock_ = timeline() && epoch_set_ ? cycles - epoch_ : cycles;
+   }
+
+   virtual void setArmed(unsigned long cycles) { armed_clock_ = cycles; }
+   virtual unsigned long lateCycles() { unsigned long l = late_; late_ = 0; return l; }
+
+   virtual unsigned char send(unsigned char data, bool fastCgb)
+   {
+      if (timeline()) return time_send(data, fastCgb);
+      if (!active())
+         return 0xFF;                   /* nobody on the other end yet */
+      unsigned seq = seq_ = (seq_ + 1) & 0xFFFF;
+      unsigned gap = HB_NP_GAP_NONE;
+      if (last_xfer_clock_ && clock_ >= last_xfer_clock_ && (clock_ - last_xfer_clock_) / HB_NP_GAP_UNIT < HB_NP_GAP_NONE)
+         gap = (unsigned)((clock_ - last_xfer_clock_) / HB_NP_GAP_UNIT);
+      last_xfer_clock_ = clock_;        /* this Game Boy is paused until the answer: the next gap counts from here */
+      if (after_send_)
+         turn_seen_ = false;            /* v4bw: it did not answer our last byte with one of its own */
+      /* v4bw: sending now. If the other side answered our last byte with a byte of its own
+       * (Monster Capsule GB: the two take turns as master, and the one listening gives up after
+       * 262144 cycles), stop and wait for that byte once this side ran one 240 Hz tick, instead
+       * of running on: catching up a few frames at once after a slow answer, it timed out before
+       * the other side's byte came ('통신 오류입니다'). The hold in check() then takes the byte at
+       * its own time. Its gaps vary (1334 to 9777 units within one exchange), so not from them.
+       * Otherwise not waiting. */
+      expect_ = turn_seen_ ? (unsigned long)HB_NP_GAP_NEW * HB_NP_GAP_UNIT + 1 : 0;
+      after_send_ = true;
+      put('Q', seq, data, fastCgb ? 1 : 0, gap);
+      unsigned long deadline = now_ms() + HB_NP_TIMEOUT_MS;
+      bool crossed = false;
+      for (;;) {
+         for (unsigned i = head_; i != tail_; i = (i + 1) & (HB_NP_QUEUE - 1)) {
+            Unit &u = q_[i];
+            if (u.type == 'R' && u.seq == seq) {
+               unsigned char got = u.data;
+               u.type = 0;
+               drop_used();
+               tr("gotR", seq, got, 0);
+               return got;              /* the other side's answer */
+            }
+            if (u.type == 'Q') {
+               /* v4bw: both started a transfer. On a cable one starts first and the other,
+                * a master itself by then, is not listening, so the host's byte goes first:
+                * the client answers it with FF and waits for its own answer; the host keeps
+                * the client's byte for when it listens. (v4bv gave each the other's byte, and
+                * two Game Boys retrying a call on the same beat crossed every time: Monster
+                * Capsule GB '통신 준비가 되어 있지 않습니다'.) */
+               if (!is_host_) {
+                  put('R', u.seq, 0xFF, 128, 0);
+                  u.type = 0;
+                  tr("crossQ-ff", u.seq, u.data, seq);
+               } else if (!crossed) {
+                  crossed = true;
+                  tr("crossQ-keep", u.seq, u.data, seq);
+               }
+            }
+         }
+         drop_used();
+         if (!active())
+            return 0xFF;                /* the other player left */
+         if (now_ms() > deadline) {
+            tr("timeout", seq, 0, 0);
+            put('C', seq, 0, 0, 0);
+            gambatte_log(RETRO_LOG_INFO, "GB link over netplay: no answer from the other Game Boy for %d ms, sent 0xFF\n", HB_NP_TIMEOUT_MS);
+            return 0xFF;
+         }
+         poll_fn_();
+         if (head_ == tail_)
+            sleep_us(200);
+      }
+   }
+
+   virtual bool check(unsigned char out, unsigned char& in, bool& fastCgb)
+   {
+      if (timeline()) return time_check(out, in, fastCgb);
+      if (!active())
+         return false;
+      if (head_ == tail_) {
+         if (expect_ && clock_ >= last_xfer_clock_ && clock_ - last_xfer_clock_ >= expect_
+               && clock_ - last_xfer_clock_ <= expect_ + HB_NP_LATE) {
+            /* The other Game Boy kept this gap before its last byte, so its next one
+             * is due now: wait for it here with this game paused. */
+            unsigned long deadline = now_ms() + HB_NP_WAIT_MS;
+            for (;;) {
+               poll_fn_();
+               if (!active())
+                  return false;
+               if (head_ != tail_)
+                  break;
+               if (now_ms() >= deadline) {
+                  tr("waitend", 0, 0, 0);
+                  expect_ = 0;          /* it did not come: back to plain polling */
+                  return false;
+               }
+               sleep_us(200);
+            }
+         } else {
+            unsigned long t = now_ms();
+            if (t == last_poll_ms_)
+               return false;            /* RetroArch also reads packets every frame; this only shortens the wait */
+            last_poll_ms_ = t;
+            poll_fn_();
+            if (!active())
+               return false;
+         }
+      }
+      while (head_ != tail_) {
+         Unit u = q_[head_];
+         if (u.type != 'Q') {
+            head_ = (head_ + 1) & (HB_NP_QUEUE - 1);
+            continue;                   /* stale answer, nobody waits for it */
+         }
+         /* The frontend batches frames; exact first-byte phase is unavailable.
+          * Keep the remaining gap, including for the second byte, but do not
+          * apply this allowance to a direction change after our own send.
+          * guess_gap() consumes this one-shot state when the byte is accepted. */
+         unsigned long late = 0;
+         if (u.gap != HB_NP_GAP_NONE && last_xfer_clock_ && clock_ >= last_xfer_clock_) {
+            unsigned long due = (unsigned long)u.gap * HB_NP_GAP_UNIT, ran = clock_ - last_xfer_clock_;
+            bool slack = hist_n_ == 0 && !after_send_ && u.gap < HB_NP_GAP_LONG;
+            if (slack)
+               due = due > HB_NP_STARTUP_SLACK ? due - HB_NP_STARTUP_SLACK : 0;
+            if (ran < due && due - ran <= HB_NP_CATCHUP) {
+               if (u.seq != held_seq_) {
+                  held_seq_ = u.seq;
+                  tr("hold", u.seq, u.data, (unsigned)((due - ran) / HB_NP_GAP_UNIT));
+               }
+               return false;
+            }
+            /* v4bw: the byte was on the wire when 'due' passed (this side armed by then),
+             * not when this check came: count from then so the lateness does not pile up. */
+            if (!slack && u.gap < HB_NP_GAP_LONG && ran > due) {
+               late = ran - due;
+               if (armed_clock_ > clock_ - late)
+                  late = armed_clock_ < clock_ ? clock_ - armed_clock_ : 0;
+               if (late > HB_NP_POLL_LATE)
+                  late = 0;             /* really late (the other side or this one was busy): as before */
+            }
+         }
+         head_ = (head_ + 1) & (HB_NP_QUEUE - 1);
+         in      = u.data;
+         fastCgb = (u.flag & 1) != 0;
+         tr(late ? "ansQlate" : "ansQ", u.seq, u.data, late ? (unsigned)late : u.gap);
+         put('R', u.seq, out, 128, 0);
+         last_xfer_clock_ = clock_ - late;
+         late_ = late;
+         bool turn = after_send_ && u.gap < HB_NP_GAP_LONG;
+         if (turn)
+            turn_seen_ = true;          /* v4bw: see send() */
+         after_send_ = false;
+         expect_ = turn ? 0             /* its turn soon after ours: its next byte follows our next one */
+                        : (unsigned long)guess_gap(u.gap) * HB_NP_GAP_UNIT + 1;
+         return true;
+      }
+      return false;
+   }
+
+virtual void service(unsigned long cycles, unsigned char out, unsigned char sc)
+   {
+      if (!timeline()) { unarmed(cycles, sc); return; }
+      if (!active()) return;
+      if (!epoch_set_) { epoch_=cycles; epoch_set_=true; debugState("epoch-established"); }
+      setClock(cycles);
+      if (!sent_progress_ || clock_ - sent_clock_ >= 32768) {
+         put('P', 0, out, sc, 0);
+         sent_clock_ = clock_; sent_progress_ = true;
+      }
+      poll_fn_();
+      // Let the lagging machine catch up. A queued request is serviced first,
+      // including a request from a peer currently blocked inside send().
+      unsigned long deadline = now_ms() + HB_NP_TIMEOUT_MS;
+      while (active() && (!peer_seen_ || clock_ > peer_clock_ + 70224) && head_ == tail_) {
+         poll_fn_();
+         if (now_ms() >= deadline) { tr("lead-timeout",0,0,0); break; }
+         sleep_us(200);
+      }
+      // A transfer that ended while this endpoint was not armed cannot wait
+      // indefinitely for a future receive window.
+      while (head_ != tail_) {
+         const Unit &u = q_[head_];
+         if (u.type != 'Q') { head_=(head_+1)&(HB_NP_QUEUE-1); continue; }
+         uint64_t end = u.at + ((u.flag & 1) ? 128 : 4096);
+         if ((sc & 0x81) != 0x80 && clock_ >= end) {
+            tr("unarmed",u.seq,u.data,(unsigned)(clock_-u.at));
+            put('R',u.seq,0xFF,128,0);
+            head_=(head_+1)&(HB_NP_QUEUE-1);
+            continue;
+         }
+         break;
+      }
+   }
+
+private:
+   /* Bounded session timeline, selected only for the three audited beatmania
+    * ROMs by Auto. This is byte-level compatibility, not exact clock-edge
+    * emulation. Both peers must start from corresponding game states and use
+    * the same CPU speed. Progress packets cap lead to 70224 CPU cycles plus
+    * one core event interval. A listening peer may accept a late byte; a peer
+    * observed unarmed after its interval returns FF. Internal sends overlap
+    * only when their timestamp intervals overlap. Legacy v3j remains intact
+    * for other ROMs. State loads suspend this link; explicit resets use the boot barrier. */
+   struct Unit { unsigned char type, data, flag; unsigned seq, gap; uint64_t at; };
+
+   unsigned char time_send(unsigned char data, bool fastCgb)
+   {
+      if (!active()) return 0xFF;
+      unsigned seq=seq_=(seq_+1)&0xFFFF;
+      unsigned gap=last_xfer_clock_ ? (unsigned)((clock_-last_xfer_clock_)/16) : HB_NP_GAP_NONE;
+      last_xfer_clock_=clock_;
+      put('Q',seq,data,fastCgb ? 1 : 0,gap);
+      unsigned long deadline=now_ms()+HB_NP_TIMEOUT_MS;
+      for (;;) {
+         while(head_!=tail_) {
+            Unit u=q_[head_];
+            if(u.type=='Q') {
+               uint64_t duration=fastCgb ? 128 : 4096;
+               uint64_t other_duration=(u.flag&1) ? 128 : 4096;
+               if(u.at >= clock_+duration) {
+                  tr("self-earlier",seq,u.data,(unsigned)(u.at-clock_));
+                  return 0xFF; // leave the later request for the external receive path
+               }
+               head_=(head_+1)&(HB_NP_QUEUE-1);
+               if(clock_ >= u.at+other_duration) {
+                  tr("peer-earlier",u.seq,u.data,(unsigned)(clock_-u.at));
+                  put('R',u.seq,0xFF,128,0);
+                  continue;
+               }
+               tr("overlap",seq,u.data,(unsigned)(clock_ > u.at ? clock_-u.at : u.at-clock_));
+               return u.data;
+            }
+            head_=(head_+1)&(HB_NP_QUEUE-1);
+            if(u.type=='R' && u.seq==seq) { tr("gotR",seq,u.data,0); return u.data; }
+         }
+         if(!active()) return 0xFF;
+         if(now_ms()>=deadline) { put('C',seq,0,0,0); tr("timeout",seq,0,0); return 0xFF; }
+         poll_fn_(); sleep_us(200);
+      }
+   }
+   bool time_check(unsigned char out,unsigned char &in,bool &fastCgb)
+   {
+      if(!active()) return false;
+      poll_fn_();
+      while(head_!=tail_) {
+         Unit u=q_[head_];
+         if(u.type!='Q') { head_=(head_+1)&(HB_NP_QUEUE-1); continue; }
+         if(clock_ < u.at) return false;
+         head_=(head_+1)&(HB_NP_QUEUE-1);
+         in=u.data; fastCgb=(u.flag&1)!=0;
+         tr("timeQ",u.seq,u.data,(unsigned)(clock_-u.at));
+         put('R',u.seq,out,128,0);
+         last_xfer_clock_=clock_;
+         return true;
+      }
+      return false;
+   }
+   bool active() const { return send_fn_ != NULL && peer_ >= 0 && (!timeline() || link_ready_); }
+   /* v4bw: drop answered units and stale answers at the head; a byte from the other side stays */
+   void drop_used() { while (head_ != tail_ && q_[head_].type != 'Q') head_ = (head_ + 1) & (HB_NP_QUEUE - 1); }
+   /* v4bw: a byte the other Game Boy clocked out while this one is not listening (SC not armed
+    * for an external clock) gets FF back once this side ran HB_NP_UNARMED cycles past when it
+    * was due (or first seen), as on a cable, instead of holding the sender up to HB_NP_TIMEOUT_MS. */
+   void unarmed(unsigned long cycles, unsigned char sc)
+   {
+      if (!active())
+         return;
+      drop_used();
+      if (head_ == tail_ || (sc & 0x81) == 0x80) {
+         unarmed_seq_ = 0x10000;        /* nothing waiting, or listening: check() decides */
+         return;
+      }
+      const Unit &u = q_[head_];
+      if (unarmed_seq_ != u.seq) {
+         unarmed_seq_ = u.seq;
+         unarmed_from_ = cycles;
+         if (u.gap != HB_NP_GAP_NONE && u.gap < HB_NP_GAP_LONG && last_xfer_clock_) {
+            unsigned long due = last_xfer_clock_ + (unsigned long)u.gap * HB_NP_GAP_UNIT;
+            if (due > cycles)
+               unarmed_from_ = due;     /* not due yet: this side may still start listening in time */
+         }
+      }
+      if (cycles >= unarmed_from_ && cycles - unarmed_from_ >= HB_NP_UNARMED) {
+         clock_ = cycles;
+         put('R', u.seq, 0xFF, 128, 0);
+         tr("unarmedFF", u.seq, u.data, (unsigned)(cycles - unarmed_from_));
+         head_ = (head_ + 1) & (HB_NP_QUEUE - 1);
+         unarmed_seq_ = 0x10000;
+      }
+   }
+   void clear() { clock_=0; last_poll_ms_=0; epoch_set_=false; epoch_=0; peer_seen_=false; sent_progress_=false; peer_clock_=0; sent_clock_=0; head_ = tail_ = 0; last_xfer_clock_ = 0; expect_ = 0; held_seq_ = 0x10000; hist_n_ = 0; after_send_ = false; late_ = 0; unarmed_seq_ = 0x10000; turn_seen_ = false; }
+   static bool similar(unsigned a, unsigned b)
+   {
+      unsigned d = a > b ? a - b : b - a, m = a > b ? a : b;
+      return d <= m / 8 + 4;
+   }
+   /* Remember the gap before the byte just answered and guess the one before the next
+    * byte: what followed the last similar gap, else the same gap again but at most
+    * HB_NP_GAP_NEW (waiting too early only costs a short pause, running ahead can
+    * make the game give up). */
+   unsigned guess_gap(unsigned gap)
+   {
+      if (gap >= HB_NP_GAP_LONG) {
+         hist_n_ = 0;                   /* a new transfer starts: old gaps say nothing */
+         return HB_NP_GAP_NEW;
+      }
+      if (hist_n_ == HB_NP_HIST) {
+         for (unsigned i = 1; i < HB_NP_HIST; i++)
+            hist_[i - 1] = hist_[i];
+         hist_n_--;
+      }
+      hist_[hist_n_++] = gap;
+      for (int i = (int)hist_n_ - 2; i >= 0; i--)
+         if (similar(hist_[i], gap))
+            return hist_[i + 1];
+      return gap < HB_NP_GAP_NEW ? gap : HB_NP_GAP_NEW;
+   }
+   void tr(const char* what, unsigned a, unsigned b, unsigned gap)
+   {
+      if (!trace_)
+         return;
+      struct timespec ts;
+      clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &ts);
+      fprintf(trace_, "%ld.%06ld %s %u %02x %u %lu\n", (long)ts.tv_sec, ts.tv_nsec / 1000L, what, a, b & 0xFF, gap, clock_);
+   }
+   void put(unsigned char type, unsigned seq, unsigned char data, unsigned char flag, unsigned gap)
+   {
+      if (trace_) {
+         char w[4] = { 't', 'x', (char)type, 0 };
+         tr(w, seq, data, gap);
+      }
+      unsigned char p[HB_NP_UNIT_LEN] = { type, (unsigned char)(seq & 0xFF), (unsigned char)(seq >> 8), data, (unsigned char)(flag | (timeline() ? 0x40 : 0)),
+         (unsigned char)(gap & 0xFF), (unsigned char)(gap >> 8), (unsigned char)(gap >> 16), (unsigned char)(gap >> 24) };
+      for (unsigned i=0;i<8;i++) p[9+i]=(unsigned char)((uint64_t)clock_ >> (8*i));
+      /* Preserve the complete v4bm 17-byte legacy payload for other games.
+       * Generations and boot-kind controls belong only to bounded sessions. */
+      if (timeline())
+         for (unsigned i=0;i<4;++i) { p[17+i]=(unsigned char)(generation_>>(8*i)); p[21+i]=(unsigned char)(peer_generation_>>(8*i)); }
+      send_fn_(RETRO_NETPACKET_RELIABLE | RETRO_NETPACKET_FLUSH_HINT, p, timeline() ? sizeof(p) : 17, (uint16_t)peer_);
+   }
+   static unsigned long now_ms()
+   {
+      struct timespec ts;
+      clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &ts);
+      return (unsigned long)ts.tv_sec * 1000UL + (unsigned long)(ts.tv_nsec / 1000000L);
+   }
+   static void sleep_us(long us)
+   {
+      struct timespec ts;
+      ts.tv_sec  = 0;
+      ts.tv_nsec = us * 1000L;
+      nanosleep(&ts, NULL);
+   }
+
+   retro_netpacket_send_t send_fn_;
+   retro_netpacket_poll_receive_t poll_fn_;
+   int peer_;
+   bool is_host_;
+   unsigned seq_;
+   Unit q_[HB_NP_QUEUE];
+   unsigned head_, tail_;
+   unsigned long last_poll_ms_;
+   unsigned long clock_;           /* Game Boy time (cycles) of the current check/send */
+   unsigned long last_xfer_clock_; /* Game Boy time of the last byte either way (0 = none yet) */
+   unsigned long expect_;          /* cycles after that byte when the other side's next one is due (0 = not expected) */
+   unsigned held_seq_;             /* byte held back so this Game Boy reaches its time first (traced once) */
+   unsigned hist_[HB_NP_HIST];     /* gaps of the latest bytes from the other side */
+   unsigned hist_n_;
+   bool after_send_;               /* the last byte either way was one this Game Boy sent */
+   FILE* trace_;
+   uint64_t peer_clock_;
+   uint64_t sent_clock_;
+   bool peer_seen_;
+   bool sent_progress_;
+   uint64_t epoch_;
+   bool epoch_set_;
+   bool timing_;
+   bool fresh_, boot_pending_, link_ready_, peer_boot_;
+   uint32_t generation_, peer_generation_, used_peer_generation_, peer_ack_;
+   bool boot_reset_, peer_boot_reset_;
+   unsigned long boot_deadline_, boot_tx_ms_;
+   unsigned long runs_;
+   bool auto_cold_, state_loaded_;
+   int event_;
+   bool progressed_, ever_linked_;
+   bool timeline() const { return timing_; }
+   unsigned long armed_clock_;     /* v4bw: Game Boy time this side armed SC for the byte it waits for */
+   unsigned long late_;            /* v4bw: how long the byte just taken was already due (see HB_NP_POLL_LATE) */
+   unsigned long unarmed_from_;    /* v4bw: this side's time from which the waiting byte counts as not listened to */
+   unsigned unarmed_seq_;          /* v4bw: that byte (0x10000 = none) */
+   bool turn_seen_;                /* v4bw: the other side answered our last byte with a byte of its own */
+
+};
+
+#endif
diff --git a/libgambatte/libretro/libretro.cpp b/libgambatte/libretro/libretro.cpp
index 1c4471c517b6..47c92f5bafcb 100644
--- a/libgambatte/libretro/libretro.cpp
+++ b/libgambatte/libretro/libretro.cpp
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include "bootloader.h"
 #ifdef HAVE_NETWORK
 #include "net_serial.h"
+#include "hb_netpacket_serial.h"
 #endif
 
 #if defined(__DJGPP__) && defined(__STRICT_ANSI__)
@@ -1526,6 +1527,108 @@ static NetSerial gb_net_serial;
 static SerialMode gb_serialMode = SERIAL_NONE;
 static int gb_NetworkPort = 12345;
 static std::string gb_NetworkClientAddr;
+
+/* Hanbang: GB link cable over a netplay room (hb_netpacket_serial.h) */
+static NetpacketSerial gb_np_serial;
+static bool gb_np_audited_beatmania = false;
+static uint32_t hb_np_crc32(const void *data, size_t size)
+{
+   const unsigned char *p = static_cast<const unsigned char *>(data);
+   uint32_t crc = 0xFFFFFFFFu;
+   for (size_t i=0; i<size; ++i) {
+      crc ^= p[i];
+      for (unsigned k=0; k<8; ++k)
+         crc = (crc >> 1) ^ (0xEDB88320u & (0u - (crc & 1u)));
+   }
+   return ~crc;
+}
+
+
+static void apply_serial_mode(void)
+{
+   if (gb_np_serial.started())
+   {
+      /* while a netplay room is open, the room is the cable */
+      gb_net_serial.stop();
+      gb.setSerialIO(&gb_np_serial);
+      return;
+   }
+
+   switch(gb_serialMode)
+   {
+      case SERIAL_SERVER:
+         gb_net_serial.start(true, gb_NetworkPort, gb_NetworkClientAddr);
+         gb.setSerialIO(&gb_net_serial);
+         break;
+      case SERIAL_CLIENT:
+         gb_net_serial.start(false, gb_NetworkPort, gb_NetworkClientAddr);
+         gb.setSerialIO(&gb_net_serial);
+         break;
+      default:
+         gb_net_serial.stop();
+         gb.setSerialIO(NULL);
+         break;
+   }
+}
+
+static unsigned hb_np_wait_shown = 0;
+/* UTF-8 (RetroArch font has Hangul): "GB 통신: 연결됐어요" / "GB 통신: 상대가 없어 혼자 시작 · 같이 하려면 두 기기 모두 RESET" */
+#define HB_NP_MSG_LINKED "GB \xED\x86\xB5\xEC\x8B\xA0: \xEC\x97\xB0\xEA\xB2\xB0\xEB\x90\x90\xEC\x96\xB4\xEC\x9A\x94"
+#define HB_NP_MSG_SOLO "GB \xED\x86\xB5\xEC\x8B\xA0: \xEC\x83\x81\xEB\x8C\x80\xEA\xB0\x80 \xEC\x97\x86\xEC\x96\xB4 \xED\x98\xBC\xEC\x9E\x90 \xEC\x8B\x9C\xEC\x9E\x91 \xC2\xB7 \xEA\xB0\x99\xEC\x9D\xB4 \xED\x95\x98\xEB\xA0\xA4\xEB\xA9\xB4 \xEB\x91\x90 \xEA\xB8\xB0\xEA\xB8\xB0 \xEB\xAA\xA8\xEB\x91\x90 RESET"
+static void hb_np_msg(const char *text, unsigned frames)
+{
+   struct retro_message message = { text, frames };
+   environ_cb(RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_SET_MESSAGE, &message);
+}
+
+static void RETRO_CALLCONV hb_np_start(uint16_t client_id,
+      retro_netpacket_send_t send_fn, retro_netpacket_poll_receive_t poll_receive_fn)
+{
+   gb_np_serial.start(client_id, send_fn, poll_receive_fn);
+   apply_serial_mode();
+   if (gb_np_serial.waitingForBoot()) {
+      struct retro_message message = { "GB Link: waiting for other player (20 seconds)", 180 };
+      environ_cb(RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_SET_MESSAGE, &message);
+   }
+   gambatte_log(RETRO_LOG_INFO, "GB link over netplay started (%s)\n",
+         client_id == 0 ? "host" : "client");
+}
+
+static void RETRO_CALLCONV hb_np_receive(const void* buf, size_t len, uint16_t client_id)
+{
+   gb_np_serial.receive(buf, len, client_id);
+}
+
+static void RETRO_CALLCONV hb_np_stop(void)
+{
+   gb_np_serial.stop();
+   apply_serial_mode();
+   gambatte_log(RETRO_LOG_INFO, "GB link over netplay stopped\n");
+}
+
+static bool RETRO_CALLCONV hb_np_connected(uint16_t client_id)
+{
+   bool ok = gb_np_serial.connected(client_id);
+   gambatte_log(RETRO_LOG_INFO, "GB link over netplay: player %u %s\n",
+         (unsigned)client_id, ok ? "connected" : "refused (cable already in use)");
+   return ok;
+}
+
+static void RETRO_CALLCONV hb_np_disconnected(uint16_t client_id)
+{
+   gb_np_serial.disconnected(client_id);
+   gambatte_log(RETRO_LOG_INFO, "GB link over netplay: player %u left\n", (unsigned)client_id);
+}
+
+static const struct retro_netpacket_callback hb_np_iface = {
+   hb_np_start,
+   hb_np_receive,
+   hb_np_stop,
+   NULL,
+   hb_np_connected,
+   hb_np_disconnected,
+   HB_NP_PROTOCOL,
